{"key":"u23-025-v1","kind":"mcq","model":"google/gemini-3.8-flash","pass":"solve","ok":true,"object":{"chosen_label":"D","final_answer":"lim(h→0) [(2+h)³ − 8]/h","working":"By definition, the derivative of a function f(x) at x = a is given by f'(a) = lim(h→0) [f(a+h) - f(a)] / h. For f(x) = x³ and a = 2, we have f(2) = 2³ = 8 and f(2+h) = (2+h)³. Substituting these into the definition yields f'(2) = lim(h→0) [(2+h)³ - 8] / h, which matches option D.","defect":""},"usage":{"inputTokens":419,"inputTokenDetails":{"noCacheTokens":419,"cacheReadTokens":0},"outputTokens":426,"outputTokenDetails":{"textTokens":172,"reasoningTokens":254},"totalTokens":845,"raw":{"thoughtsTokenCount":254,"promptTokenCount":419,"candidatesTokenCount":172,"totalTokenCount":845,"trafficType":"ON_DEMAND","promptTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":419}],"candidatesTokensDetails":[{"modality":"TEXT","tokenCount":172}]},"reasoningTokens":254,"cachedInputTokens":0},"attempts":1,"mode":"object","ms":4515,"keyed_label":"D"}
